  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure will center over the Upper Ohio Valley through most of \nthe work week, before slowly shifting east off the coast of New \nEngland over the weekend. The combination of the high pressure and \nstrong ridging will result in dry weather with mostly clear skies \nthrough the work week. Warm air advection as the ridge builds into \nthe region will help increase afternoon temperatures each day \nthrough the end of the week. Temperatures will warm to a few degrees \nabove normal today with highs in the upper 40s to mid 50s. Afternoon \nhighs will warm to 10 to 15 degrees above normal by Thursday and \nFriday with temperatures in the mid 50s to low 60s. Air temperatures \nof these values are more normal for early October. 850H temperatures \nin the 3C to 4C range will warm to near 9C by Thursday. It will be \nanother fantastic stretch of dry weather and above normal \ntemperatures to do outdoor work/activities. \n\nThe next potential for rain isn't expected until late Sunday, but \nthere is still a lot of uncertainty with the synoptic setup this far \nout.",
